            # --- batch 10: type-flow tier round 4 (void tail + collection-literal element typing) ---
            # A void value used as an element of an array/set literal or a key/value of a dict literal.
            VoidCollectionElement
            # A void operand of a unary `-`/`~`. Sibling of VoidOperand (which owns `not` + binaries).
            VoidUnaryOperand
            # A `match`/`catch` scrutinee that infers Void. (catch-desugared error-set matches are excluded.)
            VoidMatchScrutinee
            # A firm non-numeric (bool/string) operand of an ordering comparison `< > <= >=`. Disjoint
            # from IncompatibleComparison (`== !=`). Named operands never fire (overloadable).
            OrderingNonNumeric
            # A `for` range `A..<B` whose bound infers to a firm Float/String or Void (non-integral).
            # `actual` the offending family.
            RangeBoundNonIntegral
            # A `darray[T]` literal element whose type can't inhabit T. `expected` T, `actual` the family.
            # Disjoint from ArrayLiteralElementTypeMismatch (fixed array T[N]).
            DArrayElementTypeMismatch
            # A `set[T]` literal element whose type can't inhabit T. `expected` T, `actual` the family.
            SetElementTypeMismatch
            # A `dict[K,V]` literal VALUE whose type can't inhabit V. `expected` V, `actual` the family.
            DictValueTypeMismatch
            # A `dict[K,V]` literal KEY whose type can't inhabit K. `expected` K, `actual` the family.
            DictKeyTypeMismatch
            # A call whose callee is an identifier of Named (struct/enum) type (`p()`). `name` the callee,
            # `actual` the type. Sound: Elisa has no callable-struct/__call__ mechanism. Sibling of CallNonFunction.
            CallNamedNonFunction
            # --- batch 11: declared-shape agreement ---
            # A `match`/`Expr.Match` arm whose `Pattern.Struct` names a DIFFERENT registered struct than
            # the scrutinee's inferred struct type. `name` the scrutinee struct, `expected` the pattern struct.
            StructPatternTypeMismatch
            # A `match` arm whose variant pattern's enum qualifier is a DIFFERENT registered enum than the
            # scrutinee's enum. `name` the scrutinee enum, `expected` the arm's enum.
            MatchArmEnumMismatch
            # A `.cast[T]` that crosses the bool boundary (bool↔numeric/string/char) — never a valid
            # reinterpret. `expected` the source type, `actual` the target. Disjoint from InvalidCast
            # (numeric↔numeric value-conversion) and the allowed string↔numeric pointer cast.
            InvalidBoolCast
            # An assignment (`<-` or a compound op) to a struct field that was not declared
            # `mutable`. `name` the field. Sound: fires only when the object is a registered
            # struct AND the field is registered AND declared non-mutable.
            FieldImmutableAssign
            # First effect-system diagnostic: a `panic(...)` performed with no enclosing
            # `can`/`trusted` grant block and no signature effect grant. Warning. Sound
            # subset of stage0's effect-authority warnings — over-grants (any grant block
            # suppresses) so it never fires where stage0 is silent. See check_ungranted_panic.
            UngrantedPanic
            # A call to a uniquely-resolved function that declares signature effects
            # (`can[...]`), made at a site with no enclosing grant block. `name` the callee.
            # Warning. Same over-granting sound-subset stance as UngrantedPanic.
            UngrantedEffectCall
            # A static handler installation names an effect family that differs from
            # the family the handler declaration realizes. `name` is the handler,
            # `expected` is the handler's declared effect, and `actual` is installed.
            EffectHandlerMismatch
            # A static handler installation supplies a different number of captures than
            # the handler's ordinary leading-parameter ABI permits. `expected_count` is
            # the required count for an underflow or the total count for an overflow;
            # `actual_count` is the supplied count.
            EffectHandlerCaptureArity
            # A call to a declared abstract-effect operation that was not normalized
            # under an enclosing static handler installation.
            AbstractEffectUnhandled
            # A call to an effect-polymorphic helper that survived without a static
            # handler clone. This is a source-level effect error, not a backend decline.
            AbstractEffectHelperUnhandled
            # A static handler declares an operation that is not part of its target
            # abstract effect family.
            AbstractEffectOperationMissing
            # An effect handler declares the same operation more than once; direct
            # lowering requires one unambiguous hidden function per operation name.
            DuplicateEffectHandlerOperation
            # An abstract effect family declares the same operation name more than once;
            # zero-overhead lowering requires one unambiguous operation ABI per name.
            DuplicateAbstractEffectOperation
            # An abstract effect operation was written in an effect row. Rows name
            # operation families; operation names are valid only in call position.
            AbstractEffectOperationRow
            # A handler uses a continuation shape outside the allocation-free
            # subset. Zero-overhead handlers permit only one final `resume()`
            # in a void operation. Resumability is inferred from the syntax;
            # no handler mode keyword is needed.
            EffectHandlerResumeInvalid
            # A static handler operation has the same name as an abstract operation but its
            # parameter/return contract differs. This is a semantic error, not a backend
            # decline: static dispatch is only sound when the operation ABI is identical.
            EffectHandlerSignatureMismatch
            # A declared abstract operation was used as a first-class value rather than
            # called directly. Zero-overhead handlers have no operation closure or dispatch
            # object, so operation references must be specialized at their call site.
            AbstractEffectValue
            # An explicitly specialized abstract operation call selected a different instance
            # from the statically installed handler. The call cannot be lowered to that handler
            # without changing the operation ABI or introducing runtime dispatch.
            AbstractEffectSpecializationMismatch
            # An explicitly indexed abstract operation or handler target supplied the wrong
            # number of type arguments for the declared effect family.
            AbstractEffectSpecializationArity
            # A two-dimensional effect row (`Abstract via Permission`) names an abstract
            # family that has not been declared in the current module.
            AbstractEffectUnknown
            # A source expression attempted to name the compiler-generated direct function
            # behind a static handler operation. Those names are an implementation detail;
            # exposing them would let code bypass the abstract-effect installation boundary.
            AbstractEffectImplementationAccess
            # A concrete permission carried by an effect row (`via` or a handler operation
            # grant) names a family that is neither builtin nor declared in this module.
            ConcreteEffectPermissionUnknown
            # A machine `decreases` measure whose type is not an integer (`decreases flag`
            # over a bool param). Error. `actual` carries the offending type name.
            MachineDecreasesType
            # A `mutable T[State]&` typestate parameter passed to a call whose matching param
            # is a mutable ref (so it may widen the state), with no `ensures p => <state>`
            # declaring the transition. Error. `name` the param, `expected` the function.
            TypestateWidenedByCall
            # A `mutable T[State]&` typestate parameter whose derived state is changed by a
            # top-level field write to a DIFFERENT state and not handed back (no
            # `ensures p => <state>`). Error. `name` param, `expected` fn, `actual` new state.
            TypestateNotRestored
            # A `static def` invoked at compile time (via a `static assert`) whose body
            # unconditionally calls `error(MSG)`. Error. `name` carries MSG.
            StaticError
            # A compile-time `static def` evaluation that made more than 64 nested calls
            # (runaway/too-deep recursion). Error.
            StaticEvalDepthExceeded
            # A function's `ensures p => State` postcondition is violated: the derived-state
            # flow leaves p in a DIFFERENT state at return. Error. `name` param, `expected`
            # the fn, `actual` the tracked state.
            TypestateEnsuresUnproven
            # A `requires`/`ensure` contract statement that is not among the leading
            # statements of its function body (an ordinary statement precedes it). Error.
            # Purely positional; `decreases`/`invariant`/`changes` are exempt.
            ContractNotFirst
            # An `ensure` postcondition names `result` in a `-> void` function, where `result`
            # is unbound (no return value, no param/symbol named `result`). Error.
            ContractEnsureResultVoid
            # A `dict[K, V]` whose key type K is an affine ("linear handle") struct. Error.
            # `actual` is the offending type name.
            DictKeyAffine
            # A `set[T]` whose element type T is an affine ("linear handle") struct. Error.
            # `actual` is the offending type name.
            SetElementAffine
            # Address-of was applied to a user-declared affine/linear struct value.
            AffineAddress
            # A mutable global stores a user-declared affine/linear struct value.
            AffineGlobal
            # A function parameter is a reference to an affine or affine-containing value.
            AffineReference
            AffineUseAfterConsume
            # A closure that moves a captured affine value (fuzz F12): `expected` is "call" (a
            # second call), "use" (a non-call use of the one-shot local) or "unbound" (the
            # lambda is not bound directly to a local). `actual` is the moved capture.
            OneShotClosure
            AffineMoveRequired
            AffineScopeExit
            # A `decreases` termination clause on a function that makes NO calls at all (so it
            # cannot be recursive) — the clause is unused. Warning. `name` is the function.
            UnusedDecreases
            # A `ghost` struct field with a default value. Ghost fields are verification-only
            # and erased, so a runtime initializer is meaningless. Error. `name` is the field.
            GhostFieldDefault
            GhostLocalRead
            # A `const enum X of T` whose backing type T is a known non-integer scalar. Error.
            # `name` the enum, `expected` the offending storage type name.
            ConstEnumStorageNotInt
            # A `const enum X of T` member whose literal value does not fit storage type T. Error.
            # `name` the enum, `expected` the member, `actual` the storage type.
            ConstEnumValueOutOfRange
            # A statement-position `raise` inside a function whose signature declares no
            # `error[...]` return set (docs/62 §3.3). Error. Sound: the parser records every
            # error-set function's line, so an error-set function is never flagged; a `raise`
            # buried in a sub-expression is not at statement position and is a sound miss.
            RaiseWithoutErrorSet
            # A `@region` on a value whose type is a scalar or a declared struct, enum or alias
            # (`x: i32 @r`, `p: Point @r`): a field, a parameter or a local. Such a value has no
            # region of its own. Error. `name` is the value, `actual` the region name.
            RegionAnnotationOnScalarField
            # A packed bit group (`flags: bitset:` / `layout: bitfield:`) with two members of
            # the same name. Error. `name` the duplicated member, `expected` the group field.
            DuplicateBitGroupMember
            # A struct that declares named typestates in its header (`struct X[state A | B]:`)
            # but carries no `derive state:` block in its body — the states can never be
            # assigned, so the declaration is ill-formed. Error. `name` is the struct.
            NamedStatesWithoutDerive
            ProtocolGraphEmptyFamily
            ProtocolGraphUnresolvedFamily
            ProtocolGraphDuplicateState
            ProtocolGraphUnknownState
            ProtocolGraphDuplicateEdge
            ProtocolGraphMixedDerived
            ProtocolGraphNoNamedFamily
            ProtocolConstructorUnauthorized
            ProtocolTransitionRejected
            # An explicitly state-qualified struct construction whose known literal
            # fields make that state's derived predicate false. `name` is the struct and
            # `expected` the requested state.
            DerivedStateConstructorMismatch
            # A call argument whose derived state changed after a predicate-dependent
            # field write. `detail` is the struct, `expected`/`actual` are states.
            DerivedStateArgumentMismatch
            DerivedStateResultMismatch
            DerivedStateEvidenceUnproven
            NamedStateArgumentUnknown
            UngrantedPointerCast
            DenseNodeKeyRootMismatch
            ThreadTransferStoreDependency
            ThreadTransferRegionDependency
            # A `mutable bool` local whose writes all live inside >= 2 distinct branch
            # statements at its declaring level, read after the last branch-writing
            # statement (docs/125 flow-flag lint; no stage0 counterpart). The boolean is
            # smearing state-machine state into a variable. Warning. `name` is the flag,
            # `expected_count` the number of branch statements that write it.
            FlowFlagStateMachine
            # An `if` used as a VALUE (a bare `a if c` ternary with no `else`, or a
            # docs/119 block-value tail `if` with no `else`) — a value-producing branch
            # that yields nothing on its false path. docs/125 branch totality: the
            # ternary-requires-else invariant. Parity: stage0 rejects these as the parse
            # error "expected else" (ternary) and semantic "docs/119 E7" (block-value);
            # stage1 unifies both under this one check. Error. The surviving
            # `Expr.If(_, _, Expr.Invalid)` node is the sole signature (legal guards are
            # desugared to `Stmt.If` in the parser, so none reach here).
            IfValueMissingElse
            # A `match` arm's tuple pattern has a different number of sub-patterns than the
            # tuple scrutinee has positions — e.g. `match a, b:` with an arm `(x, y, z):`.
            # Fires ONLY when the scrutinee is a tuple literal (arity known from the AST) and
            # the arm pattern is a tuple pattern of a different arity; every other shape bails,
            # so there are no false positives. Error.
            TuplePatternArityMismatch
            # An or-pattern's alternatives bind different sets of names — e.g.
            # `A(x) | B(y):`. Every alternative of an `A | B | …` pattern must introduce the
            # same binding names, since the arm body may run under any alternative. Purely
            # structural (binding names collected from the AST); fires only when two
            # alternatives' name SETS differ, so no false positives. Error.
            OrPatternBindingMismatch
            # A membership test `x in RHS` whose right-hand side is a CONTAINER-typed
            # value — stage0 requires a list literal or tokenset on the right of `in`
            # (parity: "membership operator requires a list literal or tokenset on the
            # right-hand side, got darray[...]"). Fires only on a firm structural
            # Container (annotated local / registered field / unique call). Error.
            MembershipRhsContainer
            # A `xs.push(v)` on a darray-typed value whose single argument can never
            # inhabit the darray's element type (`xs: darray[i64]; xs.push("s")`).
            # `expected` the element type, `actual` the argument's literal kind or firm
            # family. Parity: stage0's "darray push expects i64, got …". Error.
            DarrayPushTypeMismatch
            # A `d[k] <- v` / `d[k]` dict access whose KEY can never inhabit the
            # dict's declared key type (`d: dict[i64, V]; d["x"] <- v`). `expected`
            # the key type, `actual` the key's literal kind or firm family. Parity:
            # stage0's "dict index expects key of type i64, got …". Error.
            DictIndexKeyTypeMismatch
            # A value-constructor call `T(x)` whose argument can never convert:
            # a container into a scalar (`i64(xs)`) or a numeric into bool
            # (`bool(3)`). `expected` the target type, `actual` the source.
            # Parity: stage0's "invalid cast from int to bool". Error.
            InvalidCtorCast
            # A MODULE name used as a value (`x = M`, `M.member` — `.` accesses
            # value members). `name` is the module. Parity: stage0's
            # "M" is a namespace; write M::member. Error. Fires only when every
            # symbol of that name is a Module and no local/param shadows it.
            NamespaceUsedAsValue
            # `M::Unknown` where M IS a module but declares no `Unknown`. stage0 spells it
            # `undefined identifier "M.Unknown"`; name = module, expected = member.
            UndefinedModuleMember
            # `r <- v` where `r` is a non-`mutable` local whose type is a plain `T&` that is
            # NOT a write-through binding (see resolve.elisa `collect_ref_locals_to_skip`).
            # stage0: `cannot assign through readonly ref "r"` followed by a separate note
            # line (`ReadonlyRefAssignNote`). name = local, expected = base type.
            AssignThroughReadonlyRef
            # The note stage0 prints right after AssignThroughReadonlyRef, as its own line:
            # `note: plain refs T& are readonly; use mutable T& if this reference should
            # allow writes`. expected = base type.
            ReadonlyRefAssignNote
            # A call argument whose aggregate state (`Holder[?]`, the default for a bare
            # `Holder` value) is not assignable to the parameter's (`Holder[&]`). stage0:
            # `argument N to "f" expects Holder[&], got Holder[?]`. name = callee, expected =
            # struct name, expected_count = argument number, actual_count = the parameter's
            # state code, detail_code = the argument's state code (see function_param_state_code).
            AggregateStateArgMismatch
            # A packed-enum move destructure explicitly names a Store belonging to a
            # different packed enum. `expected` is the moved enum owner and `actual`
            # the store's enum owner.
            PackedMoveStoreMismatch
            # A record update `value{field = replacement}` names a field absent from the
            # firmly-known registered struct type of `value`. `name` is the field and
            # `expected` is the struct name. Error.
            RecordUpdateUnknownField
            # `%` with a firmly-known float operand. Elisa modulo is integral-only.
            ModuloOperandNonIntegral
            # A POSITIONAL container — array or darray — indexed by a firmly-known float
            # value. `actual` is the offending index type, spelled as stage0 spells it
            # ("f64", not the "float" family).
            ArrayIndexNonIntegral
            # A for-loop range whose explicit literal stride is zero.
            RangeStepZero
            # A consuming `move value as Struct(...)` positional destructure has a
            # different binding count from the registered struct field count.
            MoveStructPatternArityMismatch
            # An anonymous `let {field}` destructure selects a field absent from the
            # firmly-known struct type of its right-hand side.
            LetDestructureUnknownField
            UnknownFunctionAnnotation
            UnknownExternFunctionAnnotation
            TestFunctionParameters
            BenchFunctionNonVoidReturn
            GenericFixtureFunction
            AnnotatedFunctionPermissions
            GuardNonnullNonOptionalParam
            ProtocolRequiresConcreteType
            GenericInterfaceBoundUnsatisfied
            GenericOperatorNoBound
            ExternBorrowUnknownParam
            ExternBorrowNonProvenanceParam
            ExternBorrowFieldNonStructReturn
            ExternBorrowUnknownReturnField
            ThreadArgumentNotShareable
            ThreadResultNotShareable
            ArraySliceEndOutOfBounds
            ArraySliceReversed
            RuntimeArraySize
            FixedArrayShapeMismatch
            ReadonlyViewIndexAssign
            StringViewIndexAssign
            StringIndexAssign
            MutableViewFromReadonlySource
            MutableIterationReadonlyView
            UnknownRegionBacking
            RegionLinearAllocation
            # A `@region` on a fixed array (`xs: array[i64, 4] @r`), which has no region field.
            # Error. stage0 words this apart from RegionAnnotationOnScalarField: `actual` the
            # region, `expected`/`detail`/`expected_count` the element and length, and
            # `detail2`/`detail3`/`actual_count` the same for a fixed-array element.
            RegionAnnotationOnFixedArray
            UnknownRegionQualifier
            RegionQualifierMismatch
            LocalRegionReferenceEscape
            RegionParamInferenceFailure
            # stage0's text for a CONDITIONAL alias of a grown parameter (`v = p.name if c else "x"`,
            # then `return v`): the implicit region `__rg_<name>` reads as scope-owned there.
            ScopeOwnedRegionReturnEscape
            EmptyArrayWithoutContext
            LegacyCastCallSyntax
            RemovedRefShorthand
            RemovedPackedAbiAnnotation
            RemovedPackedPrefixAnnotation
            RemovedCbindPrefixAnnotation
            UnknownStructAnnotation
            UnknownEnumAnnotation
            InlineAnnotationArity
            InlineAnnotationMode
            AlignAnnotationArity
            AlignAnnotationValue
            FixedLayoutAnnotationArguments
            PackedProfileAnnotationNotPacked
            PackedProfileAnnotationArity
            PackedProfileAnnotationMode
            OptionalComparison
            CopyRuntimeLength
            CopyScalarTarget
            CopySizeMismatch
            ForwardingVariadic
            IdUnwrapNonId
            ReadOnlyViewAssign
            RowIdNonSoa
            SparseRequiresSoa
            IterCalleeMutableRef
            LawSubjectTypeMismatch
            RefinementSubjectMismatch
            CBindRequiresCLayout
            PackedStoreIndexAssign
            PackedConstructorWithoutStore
            PackedFrozenStoreAllocation
            PackedMatchMissingStore
            OrdinaryMatchWithStore
            OrdinaryEnumBareVariantType
            NamedPatternOnUnnamedPayload
            ErrorConstructorArgumentType
            NumericLiteralSuffix
            AmbiguousBareRange
            AssignScalarToContainer
            # A bare parallel rebind whose threading `lmut` call consumed a target (stage0's
            # tuple-to-one-target and arity readings; check_parallel_rebind_threading).
            ParallelRebindThreadedTuple
            TupleDestructureArityMismatch
            # An owned container allocated in a `region` block and returned from it (§3.3.7):
            # stage0's two findings, at the returned name and at `return`.
            RegionValueEscapesReturn
            RegionReturnDependency
            WildcardArmNotFinal
            DerivedStateRuleNotFieldBased
            DarrayPushImmutableReceiver
            DarrayPushArenaRequired
            CountingFillUnreserved
            RegionParamUninferable
            AssertProofHole
            AssertExplicitHole
            TupleIterableNotTuple
