            # inside a loop after an in-loop element read of it, widening what that read (checked
            # only against the elements added before it) may see on a later iteration.
            # The second line stage0 prints for a store whose INTERIOR dangles: `expected` names the
            # carrier ("fresh container"), `name` the parameter whose region `__rg_<name>` outlives it.
            RegionStoreEscapeVia
            LoopElementReadWidened
            # A closure passed to a task-submission (`submit`) captures a by-value/ref binding
            # that owns heap state (a container, or a struct/ref with a container member); the
            # captured state cannot outlive the async task. `name` the submit target function.
            ClosureCaptureEscape
            # An index expression uses a local bound to a call to a signed-integer function
